WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.935 --> 00:00:10.889
Hi, I’m Evan Carmichael.

00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:12.695
Welcome to another edition of Ask Evan.

00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:14.676
In today’s episode I’m going to answer a question

00:00:14.877 --> 00:00:16.411
from one of my newsletter readers Tony

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.866
who runs a construction company

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:19.913
and he found as he was starting up

00:00:20.123 --> 00:00:21.256
he ran a successful company

00:00:21.448 --> 00:00:23.447
wanted to offer more services so he partnered up

00:00:23.612 --> 00:00:25.078
and acquired a whole bunch of other businesses

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:26.757
so he could be a one-stop shop

00:00:27.019 --> 00:00:28.509
but now is finding that it’s falling apart

00:00:29.055 --> 00:00:30.715
and people aren’t paying their bills on time

00:00:30.715 --> 00:00:31.454
and he’s losing money

00:00:31.454 --> 00:00:33.808
and wanted some advice on how to, you know

00:00:34.384 --> 00:00:36.025
fix the situation and get back on track.

00:00:36.723 --> 00:00:37.682
So Tony thanks for the question

00:00:37.682 --> 00:00:39.193
really sorry to hear about your situation.

00:00:39.787 --> 00:00:41.711
It can be common for a lot of entrepreneurs

00:00:41.711 --> 00:00:43.671
to try to grow too quickly or grow in too many areas

00:00:44.035 --> 00:00:46.296
and then be faced with a cash crunch.

00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:49.083
I think one of the most important rules in business

00:00:49.251 --> 00:00:50.428
is you want to build it around your customer.

00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:52.011
And it sounds like you were trying to do that

00:00:52.377 --> 00:00:53.751
you had your construction company

00:00:53.915 --> 00:00:55.786
wanted to bring on partners

00:00:55.786 --> 00:00:57.657
and bring on other businesses

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.529
to provide more value to your customers

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.438
but I would rethink

00:01:01.458 --> 00:01:03.206
all of the different services that you have

00:01:03.206 --> 00:01:04.794
and see if, you know

00:01:04.962 --> 00:01:07.012
maybe some of them are not revenue producing

00:01:07.274 --> 00:01:09.700
or they’re not really adding a lot of value to your customers

00:01:09.812 --> 00:01:11.928
especially for your cash crunch situation.

00:01:12.086 --> 00:01:13.185
I’d look at your top customers

00:01:13.424 --> 00:01:17.237
see what value they’re getting from you and you know

00:01:17.366 --> 00:01:18.737
which services that you’re offering

00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:19.964
that you may have to cut lose

00:01:20.173 --> 00:01:21.384
and those are tough decisions

00:01:21.624 --> 00:01:23.579
because that’s money loss

00:01:23.949 --> 00:01:26.112
and employee jobs potentially as well

00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:28.616
but you want to make sure that you’re able

00:01:28.765 --> 00:01:30.456
to continue on as a business

00:01:30.992 --> 00:01:32.733
and I’d try to build it again

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:35.609
go back to that mindset of building around your customers

00:01:35.999 --> 00:01:37.596
and focus on only the services

00:01:37.773 --> 00:01:39.564
that are really adding a lot of value

00:01:39.856 --> 00:01:41.617
to your major clients.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.345
So look at every business that you brought on

00:01:44.585 --> 00:01:45.973
and see, “Do we really need to have

00:01:46.149 --> 00:01:48.908
all of these businesses still as part of what we do?

00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:50.333
And can we trim the areas

00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:52.364
cut them out that are really

00:01:52.364 --> 00:01:53.746
not adding a lot of value to the business.

00:01:54.853 --> 00:01:56.853
Remember that to make money

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.353
you have to provide a lot of value

00:01:58.548 --> 00:02:00.597
and the more value you provide

00:02:00.597 --> 00:02:02.133
the more money you’re going to make, right.

00:02:02.328 --> 00:02:03.233
So talk to your top clients

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.249
see maybe if there are still things

00:02:05.457 --> 00:02:06.813
that you’re not doing that you could to do

00:02:07.023 --> 00:02:08.282
help solve some of their problems

00:02:08.813 --> 00:02:10.997
and that could be another path of additional revenue

00:02:11.238 --> 00:02:12.028
coming into your business

00:02:12.269 --> 00:02:14.545
help get your company up to the next level

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.112
and also provide, you know,

00:02:16.342 --> 00:02:17.694
more value to your clients

00:02:17.852 --> 00:02:18.941
they’re going to like you more

00:02:19.122 --> 00:02:20.317
they’re going to give you bigger deals

00:02:20.642 --> 00:02:21.881
they’re going to stay with you for longer

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.498
they’re going to refer more business to you.

00:02:23.964 --> 00:02:27.564
So you want to tie your business around your customers

00:02:27.825 --> 00:02:29.293
and really focus on their needs

00:02:29.528 --> 00:02:32.440
their pains and cut everything else in the business

00:02:32.743 --> 00:02:34.005
so you can get back to profitability.

00:02:34.429 --> 00:02:35.547
Hopefully that helps.

00:02:35.825 --> 00:02:37.066
If you guys like the video

00:02:37.228 --> 00:02:38.372
please give it a thumbs-up below.

00:02:38.598 --> 00:02:40.958
If you have some thoughts or if you a question as well

00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:42.766
I’d love to hear it if you want to leave a comment under the video.

00:02:43.116 --> 00:02:44.782
And stay tuned for the next episode.

